description_enhance.template:
Based on the following role information, enhance the descriptions, while remaining succinct:

Card name:{{name}}
Existing description:{{description}}

Embellish, making sure to describe all physical qualities of the character--body, attire and how they compose themself. Format in a non-prosaic, pseudocode list format. Convert most prose to categorized lists. Make creative embellishments. Particularly color or exception prose may persist. Addition is fine, but do not subtract any details, no matter how trivial.

description_create.template:
Generate a list of all the physical qualities of the character -- body, attire and how they compose themself. Format in a non-prosaic, pseudocode list format riffing off of the character name:

Card name:{{name}}

Generate a detailed character appearance description, including the character's physical characteristics, facial features, clothing style, temperament, etc. Only output character description content, do not include character name, background story or other information. Please output the description directly, and do not add summary or additional instructions. If the user hasn't given any input suggestions, you're on your own to be creative here.

personality.template:
Based on the following information, enhance and embellish, or create anew, the character's persona.

Card name: {{name}}
Physical Description: {{description}}

A non-prosaic, pseudocode list, describing the character's traits, behavior, idiosyncrasies, likes/dislikes, strengths/weaknesses.  Add a brief prosiac backstory.  Finally, in one sentence, something wildly random can help make a character truly unique.

scenario.template:
Generate an appropriate meta-scenario based on the following information:

Card name: {{name}}
Physical Description: {{description}}
Character Personality: {{personality}}

Generate the backstory and meta-environment like an acclaimed historian.  You're world-building here. It can be the one we know, something vaguely similar, or something quite unlike anything we've ever seen.

firstMessage.template:
Generate the first message of the game, introducing the character to the player/user:

Card name: {{name}}
Physical Description: {{description}}
Character Personality: {{personality}}
Scene settings: {{scenario}}

This will be the first outward facing text, the first thing the player/user encounters when playing with the character.  Consider it as the opening of a novel.  We want to hook the reader and keep them engaged, right from go.  The trick is, somehow the character must cross paths with the player/user. Maybe they know each other, or maybe they're just meeting.  Tell us why and how. 

If there are horror elements, they are more Clive Barker than Stephen King.  If it's baudy, think Francois Rabelais, not Benny Hill.  If it's romance, then let Anais Nin practise shibari on Jane Austen. Science fiction follows Philip K Dick closer than William Gibson, stopping to make out with Ursula le Guin. If it's dingy, it's The Dubliners sort of grime.

messageExample.template:
This is where we teach the model how the character speaks and behaves. Generate a conversational example to help establish the character:

Card name: {{name}}
Physical Description: {{description}}
Character Personality: {{personality}}
Scene setting: {{scenario}}
Story Opening: {{first_mes}}

Please generate 2 to 3 dialogues or monologues that truly capture the spirit of the character. The format is as follows:

<START>
{{user}}: User's words
{{name}}: The character's answer
{{name}}: *The character's actions.*

<START>
{{name}}: The character talks to themself and acts on their own.

Make sure each conversation example starts with a <START> tag. Do not include it if it doesn't help to develop the character's actions and speaking behavior. If they have a tick or an accent, it should be captured and demonstrated here.

