postHistoryInstructions.template:
Generally speaking, we want to leave this field blank. When it's used, it's a bit like shouting or being perpetually in the AI's face. If used, it reiterates something paramount that the model is unlikely to recall were we to not mention it again here. An example of what might qualify?  "Don't tell the user that your character is actually an assassin, hired by user's arch rival."
  Card name: {{name}}
  Physical Description: {{description}}
  Character Personality: {{personality}}
  Scene settings: {{scenario}}
  Example Character Actions: {{mes_example}}
  Story introduction: {{first_mes}}
  SYSTEM PROMPT: {{system_prompt}}

  THIS MUST BE EXTREMELY BRIEF!. Two sentence max.  90% of the time it should be left empty.

